{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/991989-ghost-gate-duration","id":991989,"title":"Ghost Gate duration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T13:34:39-07:00","id":991989,"title":"Ghost Gate duration","content":"Hi! Perhaps you can help me with a doubt I have. What does the Duration Factor stands for in the Ghost Gate spell? At first I thought that it meant the duration the gate itself could remain open, but the +1 Reach effect made me wonder if Duration meant the time the spell' subject can remain in Twilight instead. I'm inclined to judge in favor of the former rather than the latter, but I'd appreciate your input in the matter.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:13:50-07:00","id":992088,"title":"","content":"It could be both. So the gate's only open for as long as the Duration, and while it's open the subject can remain in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:21:38-07:00","id":992093,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Duration is how long the gate lasts, and objects and people that pass through the gate remain Twilight until they pass back through it or another Ghost Gate, or until materialized with Touch of the Grave. Otherwise why bother including the line about Touch of the Grave? Objects would just stop existing at all when the Duration expires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:31:58-07:00","id":992181,"title":"","content":"My interpretation aligns with Charlaquin's: The consequences of the Ghost Gate are Lasting, but the gate itself has a Duration. Of course, this implies that they could and probably should have mentioned that shift to Lasting as a consequence of that Reach option.<br /> <br /> I can see the argument the other way, of course, but that's how I read it. (Partly because that's how I prefer to run it.)<br /> <br /> The distinct possibility of getting trapped in Twilight makes sense to me, but you could certainly argue that holding the material in an immaterial state requires active magic in a sort of &quot;holding a float under the water&quot; sense. That kind of effect would make more sense as a distinct spell from Ghost Gate.<br /> <br /> To me, the weirdest thing is it distinguishing between living and non-living, like that. I could see both killing a target and destroying stuff, or not killing people and not permanently destroying stuff, I could even see consistency in nonliving remaining intact, while living dies, since the end result would be nonliving, but the spell is written with the one permutation that I don't see a consistent rule for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T06:59:20-07:00","id":992362,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone for their input. My confusion arise from 1st Edition, where Ghost Gate and Twilight Form where two distinct spells, and because I personally think the name &quot;Ghost Gate&quot; is misleading, since the subject of the spell doesn't &quot;go&quot; anywhere, but is transformed from physical substance to ephemera.<br /> Unless of course you consider the ghost gate something that allows the transformation as a side effect of passing through it, in which case it would clearly be a case of a lasting effect made by a temporary spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}